From: Yoram van de Velde <yoortje@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] android: tune the network read cache in advancedsettings

Playback from the WebDAV source stutters. Kodi's default cache is small and
only buffers the local sources it knows are slow, so any latency spike on the
server side (disk, CPU throttling of the WebDAV pod) shows up directly as a
stall.

Enable buffering for network filesystems (buffermode 1), raise the memory
cache to 150 MiB and read ahead more aggressively (readfactor 20). The file is
rewritten from this template on every start (see Splash.java), so editing the
copy on the device does not stick; the values have to live here.
---
 userdata/advancedsettings.xml.in | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/userdata/advancedsettings.xml.in b/userdata/advancedsettings.xml.in
index d7e78b48c9..0000000000 100644
--- a/userdata/advancedsettings.xml.in
+++ b/userdata/advancedsettings.xml.in
@@ -1,4 +1,9 @@
 <advancedsettings>
+  <cache>
+    <buffermode>1</buffermode>
+    <memorysize>157286400</memorysize>
+    <readfactor>20</readfactor>
+  </cache>
   <videodatabase>
     <type>mysql</type>
     <host>@KODI_DB_HOST@</host>
-- 
2.55.0
